,{"id":279128044,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkxMjgwNDQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/confirmed","name":"confirmed","color":"aaddaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-10-16T13:43:54Z","updated_at":"2025-10-23T20:42:13Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot Dev 4.6\nGodot 4.5\nGodot 4.0\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev1.mono - CachyOS Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 03 Oct 2025 17:06:47 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7800 XT (RADV NAVI32) - AMD Ryzen 5 5600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 31.24 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nSDFGI seemingly begins to completely ignore dynamic lights as Y values increase or decrease. The environment/sky/ambient light will still be bounced around surfaces, but dynamic lights will not create any indirect lighting.\n\nBasic room at position 0,0,0:\n\n<img width=\"1158\" height=\"645\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/972d2f2e-5dac-4d41-85c9-831d70e607e2\" />\n\nBasic room at position 0, 200, 0 (no other changes):\n\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"653\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fd760502-bed9-43f8-8638-38dec01c6a74\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a small room with a high energy spotlight and a camera (character controller optional). Mine is a StaticBody3D with mesh and collision.\n- Add a world environment, and enable the default SDFGI settings\n- If the small room is at position 0,0,0, SDFGI should work correctly, and the dynamic spotlight will bounce and create indirect lighting\n- If the room is moved to 0, 200, 0, SDFGI will completely ignore the spotlight. The same is true at 0, -200, 0\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test-sdfgi.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/22950557/test-sdfgi.zip)\n\nStaticBody3D is at 0,0,0. SDFGI will work. Setting the transform of the StaticBody3D to 0, 200, 0 should break SDFGI for the dynamic light.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111723/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111723/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}